Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||10-11-2001||09:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B> Hey, I'm currious, do any other members have HID lighting on their cars? Could it be that I ended up being the first?! (it's great, do it!)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I do believe that you are the first.  But I ordered some taillights from a site yesterday ( <A HREF="http://www.xtremewhite.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.xtremewhite.com</A>  ) who shows an H4 HID conversion kit for $700. (You'd have to already have the H4-Fiero conversion in the car for it to work, but they have it available).  Maybe someday.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||10-11-2001||10:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>Standard, I grounded mine perminately so the fan runs all the time, is this bad?  I sometimes wonder if my car runs too cool.  It seems to be going into closed loop, because I get pretty good mileage.  What do you think?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not bad, just not my preffered way.  It puts a pretty big load on the electrical system.  I like having control over when the fan coms on.. If I'm stuck in a traffic jam I just flip it on at the beginning and flip it off when I get out.<P>||||reg||1
