Z||000012||BlackStang95||10-11-2001||12:53 PM||||The only mod I've seen done in real life is 12 inch subs and 6 x 9's mounted behind each seat.  My friend (spektrum87gt) did this, built his own custom boxes and it actually turned out great, they dont move and theres still enough space to comfortably fit in either side (im no small guy either).  He mounted the amp under the box on the drivers side.  They hit incredibly hard, its actually like a punch to your back.  ||||reg||4
Z||000013||88CoupeV6||10-11-2001||02:38 PM||||I just did this one, I moved me battery to the front inside the spare tire. It is an optima battery and can be mounted at any angle because it is sealed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I used nice #1 gauge wire. I grounded to an area under the Jack on the frame & ran the + up the side of the fuel tank and to the starter.<P>I think it helps the Fiero front back weight ratio.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/battl.JPG"> ||||reg||7
