Z||000024||qwikgta||10-15-2001||10:15 PM||||I know it sounds bad in a way but I like every mod ive made, its hard to pick the best.  The Header for the 2.5 was the best for pickup, the open element air cleaner and painted valve cover for engine looks.  The homemade trunk strut was great and soooo cheap/easy.  The rims for looks, the dropped suspention and GT rear swaybar for ride and I love my short shifter too.  These would be my favs but Im always looking for the next.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<P>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html<BR>   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
